  use Ankole.DataCase, async: false

  alias Ecto.Adapters.SQL

  # Counts identify reviewed operations without parsing SQL. Changes within them still need review.
  # External.lock_identity includes the required tenant UUID in its advisory lock key.
  # InboundBatches.observed_entry_batch correlates JSON only within a tenant-scoped batch query.
  # Pod SQL binds the current tenant at every table root, join and mutation.
  # Tree and query-slot advisory keys include that tenant; set_config is local
  # to the query transaction. Copy IDs are generated by the application.
  # A drive subtree delete binds the current tenant; drive_files has no primary
  # key, so AshPostgres has no destroy action for it.
